# =====================================================
# ROBLOX CHEAT SCANNER v4.7
# PROPERTY OF JD
#
# v4.7
#   RESTORED (dropped in the v4.5 rewrite, absent for four builds):
#   * Renamed-binary scan. Reads cheat strings from inside a PE's first 64KB
#     instead of trusting its filename. v4.5 kept the helper and never called
#     it, so solara.exe renamed to svchost.exe defeated every check at once.
#   * All-time prefetch pass. The main pass honours the selected time range, so
#     a participant accepting the 2-day default hid anything older. This pass
#     ignores the range.
#   * Recent files (.lnk) -- presence class.
#   * Generic-named unsigned executables in temp -- now needs elevated entropy
#     AND no valid signature, and caps at REVIEW.
#
#   NEW:
#   * Recycle Bin $I records: original path + deletion time of deleted files.
#     Nothing evicts these automatically, unlike prefetch.
#   * Browser download history (Chrome/Edge/Brave/Opera/Firefox). Survives the
#     file being deleted, which Zone.Identifier does not. Raw string scan, not
#     a SQLite parse -- flagged REVIEW, never Critical, and the report says so.
#
#   FIXED:
#   * Bulk-deletion false positive introduced in v4.6. Any large removal was
#     CRITICAL, so Storage Sense trimming 86 of the OLDEST prefetch entries --
#     including Defender's own binaries -- read as anti-forensic cleanup.
#     Removals are now profiled: if the deleted set is full of Windows
#     servicing binaries it is CONTEXT; selective removal stays CRITICAL.
#   * Renamed $profile to $delProfile in the delta comparison; $profile is a
#     PowerShell automatic variable.
#
# v4.6.1
#   * GUI: every tab now has a detail pane. Clicking a row shows all columns in
#     full, including Evidence -- which is the column that gets clipped and the
#     one carrying the caveats that stop a finding being misread.
#   * GUI: horizontal scrolling made explicit, selection stays visible when the
#     grid loses focus, Ctrl+C copies the selected row.
#
# v4.6
#   * NEW: bulk/total artifact removal between scans is now CRITICAL on its own.
#     Per-item deletions were Context, so losing 28 prefetch entries and the
#     entire Shimcache in 13 minutes would have scored as nothing.
#   * FIXED: executor PRODUCT names in client memory were filed as grey context
#     alongside ordinary chat vocabulary. They are now REVIEW, with a note when
#     the string is short enough to occur by chance in binary data.
#   * NEW: an empty AppCompatCache is CRITICAL, not a quiet SKIP.
#   * NEW: baselines are archived to .\cheat_scan_baselines\ before being
#     overwritten. Previously every run destroyed the prior state.
#   * FIXED: declining the delta prompt left the section reason blank.
#
# v4.5.4 (patch)
#   * RESTORED: scanner self-hash (banner, report meta grid, report footer).
#     A SHA256 digest is one-way and identical on every machine running the same
#     build -- it identifies the CODE, never the operator. When the script is
#     pasted into a console instead of run from disk it now says UNAVAILABLE and
#     warns, rather than printing a placeholder that looked like a value.
#
# v4.5.3 (patch)
#   * REMOVED: scanner self-hash (was printed in the banner, the report meta
#     grid, and the report footer). Build identity now comes from the version
#     string alone. The REPORT hash is unaffected and still printed.
#
# v4.5.2 (patch)
#   * FIXED (regression from v4.5.1): the AmCache console line still referenced
#     $props after the RegistryKey rewrite, printing blank name/path.
#   * Baseline integrity warning now names the missing sidecar file.
#
# v4.5.1 (patch) -- fixes found by the first live v4.5 run:
#   * FIXED: the HTML report helper was named H(), which collides with the
#     built-in alias h -> Get-History. Aliases resolve BEFORE functions, so
#     every cell in the report called Get-History with a file path. Renamed
#     to HtmlEnc(). This is why v4.5 spewed ParameterBindingException.
#   * FIXED: AmCache hive never unmounted. The PowerShell registry PROVIDER
#     caches open key handles that GC will not release; now uses the
#     RegistryKey API with explicit Close/Dispose.
#   * FIXED: Get-WinEvent throws when a log has no matching events. Event 1102
#     reported "unavailable" (a coverage gap) when it meant "none found".
#   * NEW: mid-scan Roblox process drift is detected and reported. In the first
#     v4.5 run the client restarted between sections, so different sections
#     examined different process instances without saying so.
#
# CHANGES FROM v4.4 -- see CHANGELOG.md for the full list.
#
# HEADLINE CHANGES:
#   * Numeric scores REMOVED. Replaced with 4-state status:
#       CRITICAL (red) / REVIEW (amber) / CLEAR (green) / NOT CHECKED (grey)
#     A section that could not run now reports NOT CHECKED, never CLEAR.
#   * Term list is TIERED. Tier A = cheat-only (scores). Tier B = dual-use
#     (shown, never escalates alone). Tier C = fragment (shown, never scores).
#     Nothing was deleted from the term list.
#   * Matching is path-TOKENISED with word boundaries, and the user-profile
#     prefix is stripped, so a username can never match a term.
#   * NEW: loaded-module signer check, Zone.Identifier download provenance,
#     WER crash artifacts, launcher Modifications folder, SHA256 blocklist.
#   * Prefetch is now MAM-decompressed (run counts actually work).
#   * Handle enumeration parser fixed (was reading garbage on x64).
#
# INSTRUCTIONS:
#   FIRST SCAN  -- Close Roblox completely before running
#   SECOND SCAN -- Open Roblox, join a game, wait 1-3 min, run again
#
# Run as Administrator in PowerShell 5.1
# =====================================================

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [switch]$Unattended,
    [ValidateSet('2','3','7','all')]
